MoBetta: x87sidecar: Reduce fsin/fcos/fsincos/fptan arguments the way the x87 does.

The inline trig polynomials reduced with a 3-step Cody-Waite by true π and
documented "for |ST(0)| >= 2^23 the result is junk — accepted, no fallback".
fsin(1e18) gave 4e20, fsin(1e22) -4.24e79, and the x87's out-of-range rule
(|x| >= 2^63: ST(0) unchanged, C2 = 1) was not followed.  Stock Rosetta gets
all of it right, and goes further: it reproduces the x87's own reduction by
π rounded to 66 bits (0xC90FDAA22168C234C·2^-66), so its fsin(1e15) is 7e-7
from the true sine and 0 from that model.  Real hardware does the same.

- Reduction constant: pi_1 + pi_2 is now the x87's 66-bit π exactly
  (pi_2 = 0x1.1a6p-53, pi_3 = 0 and no longer emitted; fptan's half-π split
  likewise).  n·pi_2 is exact for |n| < 2^40, so the fast path reduces by
  the hardware's π to within rounding for |x| < 2^23.
- |x| >= 2^23, Inf and NaN leave the fast path through a flag-free guard
  (FMOV, UBFX, SUB, TBZ on the biased exponent).  2^23 <= |x| < 2^63:
  Payne-Hanek with a 129-bit window of 2^E/π66 per exponent (40 entries,
  ph_lo/ph_mid + a bit mask, 664 bytes with the two scale constants, in
  TranscendentalConstants, which still fits the loader's pad): M·T
  gives the parity of floor(|x|/π66) at bit 128 and a 64-bit fraction,
  rounded to nearest, scaled by π66·2^-64 (fptan: 2|x|/π66, π66·2^-66 for
  its half-angle).  Sign folds into the parity (sin) or the fraction (tan).
  The ADDS/ADC park the guest NZCV in a pool FPR; GPR use stays at Xconst
  plus two (Xconst is a scratch there and is rematerialised), FPR peaks
  unchanged.
- |x| >= 2^63 finite: fsin/fcos leave ST(0) unchanged and set C2 (C0..C3
  are now cleared before the body).  fsincos/fptan push at translation
  time and cannot skip it at run time as the x87 does, so they give the
  default NaN with C2 = 0; the IR tags fsincos's FSin/FCos (kTrigPaired)
  to pick that.  Inf: default NaN; NaN: quieted.
- New tests/test_trig_large.c: 9 arguments from 2^23 to 2^63 - ulp, both
  signs, against exact rationals over the 66-bit π (8 ULP or 2^-52),
  in-range C2 clear after fxam, out-of-range unchanged + C2, Inf/NaN.
  Passes under native Rosetta and the sidecar; 60 failures before.

Under Wine against stock Rosetta (tests/x87_trig_probe.c, MoBetta): every
fsin/fcos/fsincos/fptan from 0.7 to 2^63 - ulp within 1-2 ULP of the
x87 model (was off by up to 1e79), out-of-range fsin/fcos and Inf/NaN
bit-identical to stock.  Left: fsincos/fptan at |x| >= 2^63 (push and C2),
fptan of Inf/NaN pushes 1.0 where the x87 pushes the NaN (as before).

